347-
348-- Keep every opening and RESERVED cell as AIR in parts 1-2; part 4 fills openings, part 5 builds stacks after roofs cut back.
349-- Nothing crosses x12i / x12i+11 below y7; eaves and stacks above y7 stay in the plot. Run `$MCD check`, `fit --rooms`, `walk`, `light`.
100:**Plot 6 bake-oven and cistern yard (x 72..83):** ground gravel + coarse_dirt, a `dirt_path` from the gate x 77..78 straight to the pavilion and on to the oven apron. Pavilion: 6 posts `stripped_oak_log` y 1..4 at (74,7), (81,7), (74,9), (81,9), (74,11), (81,11); plates `stripped_oak_log` axis x y 4 along z 7 and z 11, ties axis z at x 74 and x 81; floor `dark_oak_planks` y 0 (flush with ground). Long table `spruce_slab` (top) on `spruce_fence` legs, y 1 over x 76..79 z 9; benches `spruce_stairs` along z 8 and z 10 (x 76..79), seats facing the table. Oven: plinth `cobbled_deepslate` y 1 x 73..77 z 14..17; brick walls `bricks` y 2..3; vault crown y 4 (upside-down brick_stairs inward + brick_slab); mouth x 75 z 14 y 2..3 open north with a `brick_stairs` upside-down lintel at y 4 over it (proud 1 at z 13 is NOT allowed: keep it in the wall line); chamber x 74..76 z 15 y 2..3 air; fire at the back x 75 z 16 y 2 (lit campfire, hay_block in the plinth y 1 under it); flue x 75 z 16 y 3..8, the stack `bricks` x 74..76 z 16..17 with `deepslate_bricks` band y 7, mouth open at y 9 (top of masonry y 8). Peel rack: `spruce_trapdoor` shelves on the stack's side x 73 y 3; flour sacks (`white_wool`) + barrels at (73,13) and (77,13). Water tank: legs `stripped_spruce_log` y 1..4 at (79,14), (82,14), (79,17), (82,17), X-braces `spruce_fence` y 2..3 between the north legs; platform `spruce_planks` y 5 x 79..82 z 14..17; staves `spruce_planks` y 6..8 ring with a `stripped_spruce_wood` hoop course y 7, interior x 80..81 z 15..16 water y 6..7; lid y 9 (see ROOFS); a `ladder` up the west side: on a `stripped_spruce_log` post at (79, 16) y 1..4 and the stave above, facing west at (78, 16) y 1..8. Spout: `spruce_trapdoor` + water_cauldron tap at (80, 13) y 1, rain barrels `barrel` facing up at (79,13), (82,13), (81,13).
